<td><FONT SIZE="1" FACE="Verdana, Arial" COLOR="#000080">Originally posted by Runmarn on 07-16-2001 01:43 PM<BR></FONT>
<TEXTAREA NAME="EditedMessage" ROWS=10 COLS=45 WRAP="VIRTUAL">I currently have the following names to join in on my proposed Runnyeye Raid. 
Kyrna (24 mage)
Jestalline (24 druid)
Shorhend’s other (16 necro)
Falabella
Dantore (25 warrior)
Badb’s other (13 rogue)
Runshad (14 SK)

I have not yet set a date for this raid because the list is too short on peeps. In order to make this work we would need a few more folks to get interested in the raid. I have run Runmarn through the zone a bit and also had a 40th season Necro friend tour the joint and with the number of caster MOBs we will need to have few more people come along. It can be worked either with a couple of back up high level buffers/healers or with two well balanced groups. As it is right now the down time for healing will be way to long to enjoy the zone. The best way to waste the place is move through in groups from one end to the other then back out again. Jlaor and I were in there a week ago to pick up the runes for my new warriors crafted armor and with Runmarn (37 ranger) running point followed in trace by Jlaor (36 druid) we went through the first 2 levels without incident. I say all this because with the endure spell buffs and my magic resist of 50, I was getting hit for plus 150 damage with some spells I would say the average casted damage was in the high 50s and up. Either way is fine by me. I just thought it would be fun to have an event geared strictly towards our lower characters so that everyone could stay in the action till they were ready to jet, and the higher level characters wouldn’t have to sit on their bums waiting for epic spawns to show up or bored sitting around waiting. 
   And the zone is currently rated at 15-35 with a 20% exp bonus
   I will give it another week before I delete this one from the board if folks aren’t that interested in doing the raid. 


Thanks for the interest from those who replied


------------------
Runmarn (HEF Ranger)
37th Season of
Surefalls


Runclar (DWF Cleric)
9th season of
Kaladim

RunShad (ISK Shadowknight)
14th Season</TEXTAREA>
